myCategory_Rank_Desc = 
RANKX(
    ALL(ecommerce[Product_Category]),
    [Total Revenue],
    ,
    DESC
)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------

RANKX(

This is a DAX function used to rank items (like categories) based on a value.

Think: “Give me the position of each category compared to others.”

ALL(ecommerce[Product_Category])

This is very important.

It means:

“Ignore any filters on Product_Category and consider ALL categories.”

Without this:

Ranking would only happen within the filtered view (wrong in most cases)

With this:

Every category is ranked against the full dataset
[Total Revenue]

This is the expression used for ranking.

It means:

“Rank categories based on their total revenue.”

So:

Highest revenue → Rank 1
Next highest → Rank 2
and so on...
, (blank argument)

This is the value argument (optional).

Since it’s blank:

DAX uses [Total Revenue] for the current row automatically
DESC

This means Descending order

So:

Highest value = Rank 1
Lowest value = Last rank

If you used ASC:

Lowest value = Rank 1
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------



Top_3_Revenue_Desc = 
IF(
    [myCategory_Rank_Desc] <= 3,
    [Total Revenue],
    BLANK()
)



Category_Rank_(Ascending)=
RANKX(
    ALL(ecommerce[Product_Category]),
    [Total Revenue],
    ,
    ASC
)

Bottom_3_Revenue =
IF(
    [Category_Rank_(Ascending)] <= 3,
    [Total Revenue],
    BLANK()
)


